  "notes": [
    "The 2007 edition covers GOLD 100 and GOLD 200; the spectral sensitivity and dye density",
    "plots are shared by both films. Kodak's own servers no longer carry it; the URL is an",
    "archive. Its GOLD 200 curves match the 2016 edition's to 0.003.",
    "",
    "Characteristic curves: daylight exposure, Status M densitometry. The sheet prints the",
    "GOLD 100 Log H ref as \"0.84\", without the minus sign: -0.84 is one stop (0.30) above",
    "GOLD 200's -1.14, as ISO 100 against 200 should be, and puts a grey card at the red",
    "density the sheet's exposure check gives for GOLD 100 (0.90 to 1.10).",
    "",
    "Page coordinates: the plots' axes are calibrated from their tick marks."
  ],
